{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope","id":1379549,"title":"Anarchs: a daring new direction or the same old trope?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-08T16:45:15-07:00","id":1379549,"title":"Anarchs: a daring new direction or the same old trope?","content":"In its premises V5 did something that I think is really cool with the Anarchs: they were lifted from a Camarilla subsect used to house malcontents and &quot;defective&quot; childer into a full sect capable to take even capital cities from the Cam (Berlin and Washington are two of the most prominent domains that come to mind, although Washington is only &quot;anarch&quot; as long as it suits Vitel's political agenda).<br /> Three great clans joined the Anarchs suddenly providing them with a lot of &quot;firepower&quot; besides their inherent advantages over the Camarilla (namely, the ability to be more &quot;In synch&quot; with the times). The Brujah and the Gangrel are probably the 2 most militant clans in the whole of VtM, while the Ministry provide access to resources mundane and arcane both.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;now&quot; the Anarchs are in the position to challenge the Camarilla, right?<br /> <br /> Apparently not. Basically all of the most recent material (most importantly Chicago by Night but also the LA by night webseries) has presented the Anarchs as they used to be . A bunch of squabbling, ineffective children on the run from the Camarilla, with powerful members of their &quot;signature clans&quot; staying loyal to the Cam (see Critias and the Wolf Pack) or going Autarkis.<br /> <br /> As far as I can see the new authors are playing it safe and presenting the old trope instead of the new one but that means V5 lacks a deeper exploration of what the new anarchs are and what they are capable of. Storytellers and players are left to their own devices when it comes to insert the new &quot;status quo&quot; into their games as the officially presented trope doesn't help turning the Anarchs into something different from what they were and even their own sect book for V5 does very little to give some structure to their way of doing things.<br /> <br /> Can we expect future products to show more of the &quot;new Anarchs&quot; are are they doomed to be presented as they always were in VtM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T16:52:59-07:00","id":1379551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope#post1379549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In its premises V5 did something that I think is really cool with the Anarchs: they were lifted from a Camarilla subsect used to house malcontents and &quot;defective&quot; childer into a full sect capable to take even capital cities from the Cam (Berlin and Washington are two of the most prominent domains that come to mind, although Washington is only &quot;anarch&quot; as long as it suits Vitel's political agenda).<br /> Three great clans joined the Anarchs suddenly providing them with a lot of &quot;firepower&quot; besides their inherent advantages over the Camarilla (namely, the ability to be more &quot;In synch&quot; with the times). The Brujah and the Gangrel are probably the 2 most militant clans in the whole of VtM, while the Ministry provide access to resources mundane and arcane both.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;now&quot; the Anarchs are in the position to challenge the Camarilla, right?<br /> <br /> Apparently not. Basically all of the most recent material (most importantly Chicago by Night but also the LA by night webseries) has presented the Anarchs as they used to be . A bunch of squabbling, ineffective children on the run from the Camarilla, with powerful members of their &quot;signature clans&quot; staying loyal to the Cam (see Critias and the Wolf Pack) or going Autarkis.<br /> <br /> As far as I can see the new authors are playing it safe and presenting the old trope instead of the new one but that means V5 lacks a deeper exploration of what the new anarchs are and what they are capable of. Storytellers and players are left to their own devices when it comes to insert the new &quot;status quo&quot; into their games as the officially presented trope doesn't help turning the Anarchs into something different from what they were and even their own sect book for V5 does very little to give some structure to their way of doing things.<br /> <br /> Can we expect future products to show more of the &quot;new Anarchs&quot; are are they doomed to be presented as they always were in VtM?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a very strange reading of the situation given the presentation of the books. I have some objections to the Anarchs treatment in THE FALL OF LONDON given that they were one of the few groups left out of the conflict between Mithras and Queen Anne. However, of the various books released, the Anarchs have had a huge role in things.<br /> <br /> * Berlin has been taken by the Anarchs. So has Indianapolis and New Zealand.<br /> * Los Angeles is now divided between the Anarchs and the Camarilla with LA by Night showing the &quot;Council of Barons&quot; is fully capable of keeping the Camarilla at bay.<br /> * The Anarchs were a major faction in Chicago by Night and the Chicago Folios.<br /> * CHAPTERS has an Anarch campaign to go along with its Camarilla one.<br /> * They killed Hardestadt with Theo Bell's defection.<br /> * There will be an Anarch campaign in Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines 2.<br /> * Coteries of New York had the Anarchs as a major faction in New York City.<br /> <br /> So what would be a better handling of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-19-2020, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T06:07:44-07:00","id":1379739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379551#post1379551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* There will be an Anarch campaign in Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are you calling Anarchs in Seattle?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T06:29:10-07:00","id":1379744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379739#post1379739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who are you calling Anarchs in Seattle?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm making a wild leap that the Baron is the Anarch leader in Seattle. Given, you know, that's an Anarch title.<br /> <br /> But I admit it could be just the criminal vampires. It would suck, though, as I felt Coteries of New York failed with its Anarch option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-09-2020, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T06:49:43-07:00","id":1379750,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs, like vampire hunters, were thematically and logistically supposed to be the underdogs, and V5 has either made great sweeping changes for a particular author's personal wish fulfillment or has flipped every power dynamic for excitement or they really like requiem (Bloodlines 2 factions are following requiem). By allowing the anarchs to gain more freedom, power and thus legitimacy, the camarilla has really picked up an idiot ball. <br /> <br /> It's an example of players not really knowing what they want. A lot of players really want the Anarchs to win, but the reason why players have wanted them to win is because they like the struggle of the anarchs, and because they like the struggle of the anarchs... it's actually better for the anarchs to lose and the Camarilla to remain an all-encompassing heel for them. The Anarchs are far more fun to play with when they're fighting an uphill battle, and whilst a lot of players have played anarch games and want to see the anarchs win because in their games they've made sweeping progress in fighting off the cam... That's an incredibly selfish mindset that does damage to the game. Imagine an underdog sports movie staring Real Madrid, or Star Wars but the Rebel alliance has half the galaxy's military and all the competent leaders. Vampire society is meant to be a long game. <br /> <br /> I also feel the new anarchs reflect reality less than they used to. In VTM, Anarchs were a vocal but struggling minority that had a few threatened territories where they actually had power. Kinda like how people non-mainstream political ideologies opperate in real life. In V5, Anarchs are equal to the Cam and aren't just a lot of noise, but where is that reality? Where are radicals making effective ground? Where aren't reactionaries winning? Are the rich not getting richer? Has social justice not been hijacked by corporatism? The Anarchs now don't actually reflect the mortal trends. They reflect someone's magical thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T07:24:52-07:00","id":1379757,"title":"","content":"i find it's less the anarchs making progress towards the defeat of the cammy's and more the camarilla shitting the bed due to the middle east situation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:24:14-07:00","id":1379817,"title":"","content":"My actual view is the Anarchs as presented are that they have gone two steps forward and one step back because the Anarchs in the game are now actually treated as less like an effective as well as organized Anarchs (ala the Carthians) and more like the Sabbat-lite. The depiction of the Anarchs in the ANARCH guide is that they're a vicious bunch of chaotic warlords as well as murderers who are on a rampage across the continents.<br /> <br /> They're doing all the same things the Sabbat were but they're capable of being inside Camarilla cities and not.<br /> <br /> So it's something that allows them to be in regular games rather than just antagonists.<br /> <br /> Thematically this works as, &quot;Here we go again!&quot; The First Anarch Revolt's mistakes are being repeated by both the Camarilla AND the Anarchs. The Anarchs are getting more vicious, more ruthless, and more psychotic--but also more effective.<br /> <br /> Then possibly when the moderates get what they want, they'll betray and the fanatics will create their own organization.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:32:43-07:00","id":1379818,"title":"","content":"Can anyone actually outline for me what the Anarch end goal is? LA By Night loves to use the Anarch Free State as a hypothetical ideal but what does that look like? A vampire society without any laws or rules where every vampire can behave as they choose is absolute chaos, as even if they don't choose to immediately break the Masquerade overfeeding or careless Embracing certainly will. But if they implement laws governed by an authority figure then it's the exact same as the Camarilla. So what's the point, what do they do and what do they want to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:48:29-07:00","id":1379822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379818#post1379818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone actually outline for me what the Anarch end goal is? LA By Night loves to use the Anarch Free State as a hypothetical ideal but what does that look like? A vampire society without any laws or rules where every vampire can behave as they choose is absolute chaos, as even if they don't choose to immediately break the Masquerade overfeeding or careless Embracing certainly will. But if they implement laws governed by an authority figure then it's the exact same as the Camarilla. So what's the point, what do they do and what do they want to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of what you're seeing is the point as the Anarchs have always been depicted as a broken organization due to the fact that they want more freedom than the Camarilla provides but this just dissolves into, well, Anarchy so that their &quot;moderates&quot; prove to be little different from the Camarilla in practice regarding. The first Anarch ever depicted in gaming was, after all, <b>Juggler</b> who was basically just a more charismatic, younger <b>Modius</b>.<br /> <br /> In general, the big difference between the Anarchs and the Camarilla is the fact that the former's leaders are generally rulers by coterie as well as chosen by small groups directly in what is a defacto democracy. It's not always that way and many Anarchs miss when they aren't. A lot of the fun of LA by Night is the fact that Annabelle is fanatically loyal to Victor despite the fact that Victor is the boss of the Valley by appointment/blackmail than any sort of mandate from the Masses (cue: Monty Python scene).<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are not the good guys but have the compelling argument of, &quot;The Camarilla doesn't serve your needs. It serves the needs of the Elders so why not kill the Elders and have a group that does serve your needs?&quot; Ideologically the two groups have a lot more in common than they will admit except for who gets the blood and the domain. The young and hungry get among Anarchs and in the Camarilla the old and corrupt.<br /> <br /> For most Anarchs, the reason they're Anarchs is because people like Lodin or La Croix want to kill or enslave them not because they have a better idea of how to run a domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-09-2020, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:01:18-07:00","id":1379824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379551#post1379551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a very strange reading of the situation given the presentation of the books. I have some objections to the Anarchs treatment in THE FALL OF LONDON given that they were one of the few groups left out of the conflict between Mithras and Queen Anne. However, of the various books released, the Anarchs have had a huge role in things.<br /> <br /> * Berlin has been taken by the Anarchs. So has Indianapolis and New Zealand.<br /> * Los Angeles is now divided between the Anarchs and the Camarilla with LA by Night showing the &quot;Council of Barons&quot; is fully capable of keeping the Camarilla at bay.<br /> * The Anarchs were a major faction in Chicago by Night and the Chicago Folios.<br /> * CHAPTERS has an Anarch campaign to go along with its Camarilla one.<br /> * They killed Hardelstadt with Theo Bell's defection.<br /> * There will be an Anarch campaign in Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines 2.<br /> * Coteries of New York had the Anarchs as a major faction in New York City.<br /> <br /> So what would be a better handling of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes, the fact that, as part of the premise of V5 Anarchs have managed to conquer whole cities, and among them some the of most relevant in the world was part of my point. That's the BACKGROUND of V5, but we've seen NOTHING of the sort besides the declaration that some cities have fallen to the Anarch movement. What we've actually seen is just the old trope, Camarilla in power and Anarchs as the underdog.<br /> 2. Los Angeles used to be the capital of the ANarch Free State. Then we had the Catayan invasion. V5 ignores the Catayans and sobstitutes them with the Camarilla. Basically the Catayans disappeared but the prince of San Diego (which also was an Anarch city taken by the Camarilla) LEFT and came to Los Angeles claiming it as his own domain. The claim is contested BUT again until season 4 what we've seen in LAbN is Anarchs being the underdog and the Camarilla having the upper hand. The way elders like Strauss (with Gargoyles apparently) and Suzanne have been presented makes every confrontation with the Camarilla in LA seem like a losing bet. And for the moment the Anarchs have suceeded to retain a fraction of the city only because they had help... from the Camarilla itself (a certain Sheriff and her previous regnant to name a couple...)<br /> 3. I don't know about the Chicago folios but in CbN the Anarchs are exactly where they were in previous editions or even worse for wear. Anyway they are not a threat to the Camarilla and are struggling to survive, which is the same old trope and basically my point.<br /> 4. I don't have chapters and I don't plan buying a boardgame but the fact there's an Anarch campaign means little by itself. What do the Anarchs do in chapters to represent the new status quo where they are supposed to present a challenge to the Camarilla instead of being a punchingbag?<br /> 5. Yes, as you may remember I pointed this out myself in a previous thread. You spent your time claiming Hardestadt was not a big deal for the Camarilla. Anyway that's like Berlin and the other cities, it's something that's supposed to have happenend in the Background of V5, not something being shown and presented by the actual game-line.<br /> 6. You don't know that. You only know the criminal elements of Seattle refer to a person called &quot;The Baron&quot; but nothing presented thus far links him (or her) to the Anarch Movement.<br /> 7. LOL. I don't want to spoil the game but... REALLY? Did you complete a playthrough? Because the actual truth puts the lie to your assertion in every conceivable way...<br /> <br /> My point is until this point V5 did nothing to move the Anarchs from their old trope to the new status quo hinted by the V5 corebook. On the contrary, until now the old trope was REINFORCED not challenged. What I want and what I'm asking for is products centered around the Anarchs presenting them in a way that makes what the corebook says believable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 04-09-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:27:23-07:00","id":1379829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379824#post1379824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is until this point V5 did nothing to move the Anarchs from their old trope to the new status quo hinted by the V5 corebook. On the contrary, until now the old trope was REINFORCED not challenged. What I want and what I'm asking for is products centered around the Anarchs presenting them in a way that makes what the corebook says believable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused but sourcebooks are always background. What would you want to show you that things have changed?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:00:57-07:00","id":1379838,"title":"","content":"I've started to see it thus. <br /> <br /> The new anarchs are basically Libertarians. They want to end the big goverment cam, so that they can replace it. The ruler doesn't have a title, just more stuff. Instead of a police force, private security or a communal funded constable (Justice for the highest bidder, either way) Second wave anarchs are actually really bad for neonates, because the Camarilla was essentially a compromise that cutailed the powers of princes with primogen councils and justicars and so on whilst allocating more thought towards the masquerade (Look how that went). By removing all of that, they're essentially opening themselves up to the old fuedal rule of the long night where, really, the prince's only threat was rebellion. If the Anarchs got their way, a hundred or so years down the line, cities will be far more tyranical than they would be under the Cam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeiss