h: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\">Washington</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Paris</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\">Ibiza (2.)</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Providence</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seattle</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">St. Louis</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stockholm</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Toronto</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tokyo (5.)</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warsaw</span></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"></td> </tr> </table></div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Hunedoara for rich neonates.</li> <li>Ashefinders and a few kindred who were there first.</li> <li>Besides Dubai, these are places in Hassan Shadid's diary in the Gehenna War chapter and I'm not sure about them.</li> <li>Albeit Bahari.</li> <li>There's odd going on there.</li> <li>Independent and supported by members of sect&quot;s&quot;.</li> <li>Camarilla and Anarchs.</li> <li>Like a cross between the Camarilla and Sabbat.</li> <li>Certainly Camarilla before Tremere attack, but a mess since.</li> <li>War zone.</li> <li>Nephilim</li> <li>Mostly thin-bloods, but apparently repopulating since SI attack; I haven't read the book.</li> <li>Hecata, but they let the Camarilla visit at least.</li> </ol><br /> The &quot;maybe Anarch&quot; column mostly consists of places where there is Anarch activity and no confirmed Camarilla presence, but it doesn't say that there <i>isn't</i> Camarilla presence. It's generally easier to identify Camarilla cities to Anarch cities, because the former have titled leaders.<br /> <br /> As for those that definitely are run by Anarchs:<ul><li>Berlin, Kharkiv and Washington D.C. are recent. The Church of Set and a Roman methusaleh were involved with the latter two.</li> <li>California and Perth went Anarch in the 20th century and the 2nd Edition, although the Camarilla has had some success returning to California in the last 25 years or so.</li> <li>To me, it seems implied that both Havana and Krakow have been Anarch run for decades.</li> <li>Tblisi was previously associated with the Soviet Brujah Council.</li> <li>Indianapolis is led by laissez-faire Ministry.</li> <li>Naples has a Rosselini Baron; it's possible that the Giovanni who were already there decided to call themselves Anarchs as a palatable way to claim authority over other kindred or that Anarchs set up shop after the Sabbat left and before the Camarilla.</li> <li>I don't know what happened in Lucerne; it might have something to do with Guillaume or his absence.</li> <li>Ibiza doesn't have leaders, formal territorities or Elysia. Apparently, the Camarilla hasn't established itself there in the first place and I don't know why not.</li> </ul><br /> In conclusion, I don't see much evidence that Anarchs have suddenly upped their game to compete with the Camarilla, but they do now have powerful allies amongst elders (I'm counting Theo Bell), clans and cults that previously had little to do with them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-09-2020, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:14:26-07:00","id":1379852,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3523\" data-vbnamecard=\"3523\">Spencer from The Hills</a> Ibiza is a partying and clubbing island, so probably Anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:24:25-07:00","id":1379861,"title":"","content":"I'm not interested in the V5 metaplot and haven't bought any of the books so keep that in mind when reading my comments. I think it's one thing to &quot;struggle against the Man&quot; when everything is about being against what X is doing (when X is Lodin, Petrodon, the Inner Circle or whatever). All that person's opponents can agree on that. It's another once one group actually seizes power and has to rule. At that point everyone's different agendas start working against each other.<br /> <br /> It is much easier for Modius. Juggler, Hinds, and Maldavis to all agree Lodin must be overthrown. But once you start discussing what the governance will look like after that, everything falls apart.<br /> <br /> So when we're talking about Anarchs seizing control of Washington, Berlin, New Zealand, Indianapolis, or whatever, what exactly are we talking about? How are the Anarchs ruling those cities? Do the other Anarchs agree? Is this really a movement coming together, or is it a movement coming apart? What does it mean that these Anarchs are ruling these cities - how is it different? How is it the same?<br /> <br /> I don't mind there being a &quot;revolutionary vanguard&quot; group within the Anarchs that could seize power. The Bolsheviks did that, of course. But the important thing to remember about the Bolsheviks is that the only way they could do it was through an unprecedented set of conditions that couldn't be duplicated. (I know the various metaplot changes in V5 is another unprecedented set of conditions, but everyone's mileage will vary). Another thing to remember is that once the Bolsheviks grabbed power, they destroyed the unity of International Socialism with most of the factions going against them, or even other radicals splitting from them. Once any group of Anarchs seize power and begin to rule, inevitably a large number of Anarchs who think differently will break from them, forcing one group or the other into a new name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:49:25-07:00","id":1379867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379852#post1379852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3523\" data-vbnamecard=\"3523\">Spencer from The Hills</a> Ibiza is a partying and clubbing island, so probably Anarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose thin-bloods do generally count as Anarchs when the Camarilla isn't openly using them and as do the permenant residents, disorganised as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-09-2020, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:52:50-07:00","id":1379869,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you\u2019re right. I forgot Ibiza was a Duskborn hangout in Cults of the Blood Gods. But they do tend to be more closely aligned with the Anarchs than the Camarilla, especially the V5 Camarilla. (Though I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if Kevin Jackson partied on Ibiza once in a while.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:22:38-07:00","id":1379878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379829#post1379829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused but sourcebooks are always background. What would you want to show you that things have changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want new books to actually give Storytellers and players scenarios where the anarchs are on the winning side. I want modules that present different type of anarch domains. We all know the LA system (a council of several barons, basically gang leaders controlling parts of the domain, consulting with each other when needed) but there are others. Washington has probably the most powerful anarch leader in the whole american continent (Vitel) what does the Washington anarch domain look like? How's it different than others? What about Berlin? The Anarchs have three great clans on their side, 2 of those were the backbone of Camarilla's military power, how does that change the Anarchs and their potential for open conflict with the Camarilla? Whatdoes it mean for anarchs to have elders joining in unprecedented numbers, how does that change the movement? Do anarchs have a superstructure, a sort of international council working to spread the movement's influence? Judging by LAbN it seems they have (Carver is working for someone after all) and even Theo Bell's actions hint there's a cohordinated effort from the anarchs to act in concert and stand up to the Cam. Unfortunately, aside from the books setting the premise for V5, modules have ignored these developments and focused on the old trope instead. I get that in some cities the Camarilla is still dominant. The problem is that was the norm. If V5 is to bring new ideas to VtM we need those ideas to be developed and at the moment besides mentioning Anarchs are resurgent that has not been a concept the game line has explored at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:46:05-07:00","id":1379969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379838#post1379838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've started to see it thus.<br /> <br /> The new anarchs are basically Libertarians. They want to end the big goverment cam, so that they can replace it. The ruler doesn't have a title, just more stuff. Instead of a police force, private security or a communal funded constable (Justice for the highest bidder, either way) Second wave anarchs are actually really bad for neonates, because the Camarilla was essentially a compromise that cutailed the powers of princes with primogen councils and justicars and so on whilst allocating more thought towards the masquerade (Look how that went). By removing all of that, they're essentially opening themselves up to the old fuedal rule of the long night where, really, the prince's only threat was rebellion. If the Anarchs got their way, a hundred or so years down the line, cities will be far more tyranical than they would be under the Cam.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day, the Anarchs are still vampires and I'm glad they're not portrayed as &quot;good guys.&quot; The Anarchs are, at best, the lesser evil and even that is sometimes not true. The Anarchs are against the Camarilla because they don't want to be oppressed but when they're in power, they're inevitably going to become oppressors themselves. The longevity, power, and influence of the Beast will corrupt all of them.<br /> <br /> Because for every Maldavis, Nines, and Anita Wainwright there's Gengis, Juggler, and Sweetie Pepper.<br /> <br /> We also have the fact that inevitably some Anarchs will defect once they get a better offer like Gordon Keaton and Damien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:57:43-07:00","id":1379974,"title":"","content":"LA by night really does a good job showing what an anarchs victory looks like. The barons each run their own domains but pressure each other into following certain rules. At least in LA it looks like most things are essentially decided city wide by baron meetings. Usually these meetings don't even include all the barons. They reference the &quot;sofa barons&quot;. Who apparently are too lethargic to do much. Some of the barons are consorting with the camarilla. Anarchs who want to get big things done have to go out and persuade people. It really reminds me of what anarchists imagined themselves doing when they invented anarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:03:22-07:00","id":1379978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379878#post1379878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want new books to actually give Storytellers and players scenarios where the anarchs are on the winning side. I want modules that present different type of anarch domains. We all know the LA system (a council of several barons, basically gang leaders controlling parts of the domain, consulting with each other when needed) but there are others.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chicago Folios showed us Joshua ruling over a small city as its Baron. Let the Streets Run Red will also detail Indianapolis which is a dual Church of Caine/Anarch domain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs have three great clans on their side, 2 of those were the backbone of Camarilla's military power, how does that change the Anarchs and their potential for open conflict with the Camarilla? Whatdoes it mean for anarchs to have elders joining in unprecedented numbers, how does that change the movement? Do anarchs have a superstructure, a sort of international council working to spread the movement's influence? </div> </div> </div>I feel like a lot of this is addressed in THE ANARCH which talks about how the fact the Brujah Council has revived itself in Russia and Cuba. It gives a lot of information in in-character fiction but it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Judging by LAbN it seems they have (Carver is working for someone after all) and even Theo Bell's actions hint there's a cohordinated effort from the anarchs to act in concert and stand up to the Cam. Unfortunately, aside from the books setting the premise for V5, modules have ignored these developments and focused on the old trope instead. </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's been that many supplements so I don't see why you feel they're being ignored.<br /> <br /> There's:<br /> <br /> * The main book<br /> * The Anarch<br /> * The Camarilla<br /> * The Fall of London<br /> * Chicago by Night<br /> * The Chicago Folios<br /> * Cults of the Blood Gods","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T03:10:50-07:00","id":1380068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1379978#post1379978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Chicago Folios showed us Joshua ruling over a small city as its Baron. Let the Streets Run Red will also detail Indianapolis which is a dual Church of Caine/Anarch domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the Chicago Folios. I reserve my judgement until I can read it but good to know, if true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like a lot of this is addressed in THE ANARCH which talks about how the fact the Brujah Council has revived itself in Russia and Cuba. It gives a lot of information in in-character fiction but it works. </div> </div> </div>Anarchs for V5 is basically a compilation of short stories with information of the Ministry, and the fact about fiction is what is said is the opinion of those who are depicted inside. For example, a lot of people here believes Samiel killed the Tzimisce antediluvian but the origin of the story is an in character piece of fiction given in the Tzimisce revisited clanbook, where the one telling the story relates the oral traditions of their clan, which unsurprisingly tend to show the Tzimisce as the most important clan of all (just to name another, the Tzimisce ante and not Caine being responsible for the Nosferatu's ante disfigurement...). Long story short, as presented that stuff is unreliable, and more to the point, it's unreliable by design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think there's been that many supplements so I don't see why you feel they're being ignored.<br /> <br /> There's:<br /> <br /> * The main book<br /> * The Anarch<br /> * The Camarilla<br /> * The Fall of London<br /> * Chicago by Night<br /> * The Chicago Folios<br /> * Cults of the Blood Gods </div> </div> </div>While it's true there's not been many supplements until now (which I think it's a good thing imo, one of the problems with the old WW system was the sheer amount of material of disputable quality that was churned out every month), one would have thought that focusing on one of the premises and fundamental differences introduced by V5 would have been a given, but it has not happened yet. Let's hope it does in the future.<br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> Let me clarify another thing: I don't want the anarchs to be presented as &quot;the good guys&quot;. I want the anarchs to live to the premises of V5 and be treated as a serious contender for the Camarilla. I want to see how the anarchs evolved in the &quot;post Gehenna&quot; scenario V5 is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T06:06:50-07:00","id":1380096,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is that the two physical books that are in print currently are set in cities that have historically been Camarilla: Chicago is &quot;The Jewel of the Camarilla,&quot; and London was historically under the control of a Ventrue Methuselah who begrudgingly tolerated Camarilla influence, or vampires who actively bought in to the system. These are both cities where Anarchs have always been underdogs. Perhaps, when &quot;L.A. By Night&quot; ends, we will get a setting book for Los Angeles, or the Free States as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T06:16:24-07:00","id":1380101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1380096#post1380096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue is that the two physical books that are in print currently are set in cities that have historically been Camarilla: Chicago is &quot;The Jewel of the Camarilla,&quot; and London was historically under the control of a Ventrue Methuselah who begrudgingly tolerated Camarilla influence, or vampires who actively bought in to the system. These are both cities where Anarchs have always been underdogs. Perhaps, when &quot;L.A. By Night&quot; ends, we will get a setting book for Los Angeles, or the Free States as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, I can't wait to read Indianapolis' write up.<br /> <br /> I really wish they'd give us a sample of LET THE STREETS RUN RED.<br /> <br /> Just one hit!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:39:38-07:00","id":1380279,"title":"","content":"I think Anarchs will fall into the same old trope if you let them. I can see enough in The Anarch to actually use the Anarchs in ways that I hadn't considered when I was playing in the 90s. I can give you an example using the campaign I am working on. In my New York City-based campaign, the Camarilla is the largest faction and exerts the most control because it's unified. The Anarchs are slightly smaller than the Cam, but are composed of different factions which are not working with the same unity of purpose as the Cam, so NYC is, in effect, a Camarilla city.<br /> <br /> THE ANARCH shows there is diversity in the Anarch mindset. And this is what I ran with, creating the following Anarch factions:<br /> <br /> Boss Callihan (from NY by Night and Coteries of New York), Baron of Staten Island: Claims to be the Baron among Barons, but his authority is being challenged by the other Barons. A Sellout.<br /> Karol Zdrada, Baron of Brooklyn: An old-school socialist who believes in authority through political councils and ideology.<br /> Reginald Yorke, Baron of The Bronx: Militant rebel. Violently protects his group from any Camarilla or outside influence. Would love to violently overthrow them.<br /> Anderson Jean, Minister of the Church of Set: Devotee of the Church and of Hesha Ruhadze. Seeks forbidden knowledge and pushes the boundaries of desires.<br /> Josephine Hebert, Regent of House Carna's New York Chapter: Carna's blood-sister, her group is aligned with the Anarchs out of convenience and opposition to the more orthodox Chantry of the Five Boroughs.<br /> Connie Perez, Baron of Harlem: Community Organizer who attempts to elevate both Kindred and Kine and is an avid follower of Salvador Garcia.<br /> Maria Rodriguez, Baron of Queens: Devotee of Agata Starek, would probably fit in with the Sabbat, minus the religious overtones.<br /> <br /> So, with these groups, you can have a rich diversity in what being an Anarch means. In fact, the strength and appeal (as well as the weakness) of the Anarch Movement is that it is so diverse. Each Baron has a very different idea of what the ideal post-Camarilla society looks like, different ideas of how to achieve these goals, and different tolerances for &quot;appropriate behavior.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T15:49:47-07:00","id":1381122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1380279#post1380279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Anarchs will fall into the same old trope if you let them. I can see enough in The Anarch to actually use the Anarchs in ways that I hadn't considered when I was playing in the 90s. I can give you an example using the campaign I am working on. In my New York City-based campaign, the Camarilla is the largest faction and exerts the most control because it's unified. The Anarchs are slightly smaller than the Cam, but are composed of different factions which are not working with the same unity of purpose as the Cam, so NYC is, in effect, a Camarilla city.<br /> <br /> THE ANARCH shows there is diversity in the Anarch mindset. And this is what I ran with, creating the following Anarch factions:<br /> <br /> Boss Callihan (from NY by Night and Coteries of New York), Baron of Staten Island: Claims to be the Baron among Barons, but his authority is being challenged by the other Barons. A Sellout.<br /> Karol Zdrada, Baron of Brooklyn: An old-school socialist who believes in authority through political councils and ideology.<br /> Reginald Yorke, Baron of The Bronx: Militant rebel. Violently protects his group from any Camarilla or outside influence. Would love to violently overthrow them.<br /> Anderson Jean, Minister of the Church of Set: Devotee of the Church and of Hesha Ruhadze. Seeks forbidden knowledge and pushes the boundaries of desires.<br /> Josephine Hebert, Regent of House Carna's New York Chapter: Carna's blood-sister, her group is aligned with the Anarchs out of convenience and opposition to the more orthodox Chantry of the Five Boroughs.<br /> Connie Perez, Baron of Harlem: Community Organizer who attempts to elevate both Kindred and Kine and is an avid follower of Salvador Garcia.<br /> Maria Rodriguez, Baron of Queens: Devotee of Agata Starek, would probably fit in with the Sabbat, minus the religious overtones.<br /> <br /> So, with these groups, you can have a rich diversity in what being an Anarch means. In fact, the strength and appeal (as well as the weakness) of the Anarch Movement is that it is so diverse. Each Baron has a very different idea of what the ideal post-Camarilla society looks like, different ideas of how to achieve these goals, and different tolerances for &quot;appropriate behavior.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what you have done, nice ideas nice execution. To keep up with canon you need to insert Torque though (and I'm pretty sure Torque will be one of the main characters to come back for this expansion. Could fit the description of your &quot;Reginal York&quot; I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:07:53-07:00","id":1381157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379549-anarchs-a-daring-new-direction-or-the-same-old-trope?p=1381122#post1381122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like what you have done, nice ideas nice execution. To keep up with canon you need to insert Torque though (and I'm pretty sure Torque will be one of the main characters to come back for this expansion. Could fit the description of your &quot;Reginal York&quot; I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Torque hasn't been seen in a while (due to events at the end of CoNY) so Yorke has taken taken his spot as Bronx Baron. I haven't forgotten about about him and Mia!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:57:34-07:00","id":1381193,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my biggest issue so far for V5 is the fact that the Anarchs didn't even get mentioned in THE FALL OF LONDON and I had to strongly rewrite the Chronicle in order to incorporate them into the city that was the Father of Punk. I really expected to have a lot more Anarch characters there but it was The Camarilla vs. The Inquisition vs. Mithras. The Sabbat even had a bit of a presence there with Monty Coven's followers but not the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> I also felt the Anarchs didn't have a very large role in CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS.<br /> <br /> Even with the defection of the Ministry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy